{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2169-01-09 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I’m Dr. Lee, one of the surgical team. You’re here today for your gastric bypass surgery, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2169-01-09 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. I’ve been preparing for this for a long time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2169-01-09 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see from your chart you’ve struggled with weight for years and tried programs like Weight Watchers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2169-01-09 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve lost weight before, but it always comes back. I want to be healthier for my family."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2169-01-09 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s completely understandable. Your BMI is 40, which qualifies as class III obesity, and surgery can be very effective."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2169-01-09 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I also have sleep apnea and acid reflux. I hope this helps with those too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2169-01-09 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It very likely will. Many patients see improvement in both conditions after bypass."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2169-01-09 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That would be a big relief. I use CPAP every night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2169-01-09 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll monitor your progress closely. Right now, we’re going to get you prepped for surgery. Any questions before we start?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2169-01-09 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I think I’m ready. Just a little nervous."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2169-01-09 08:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s completely normal. You’re in good hands. We’ll see you after the procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2169-01-09 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. You’re back in your room. The surgery went very well — laparoscopic Roux-en-Y gastric bypass and an endoscopy. You tolerated everything well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2169-01-09 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good to hear. I feel groggy, but okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2169-01-09 14:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll be on a pain pump for now — Dilaudid PCA — so you can control your discomfort."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2169-01-09 14:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I be able to eat soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2169-01-09 14:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not yet. Tomorrow we’ll start with clear liquids — that’s stage one. We’ll advance slowly to make sure there’s no leak."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2169-01-09 14:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2169-01-10 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2169-01-10 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better. My pain is manageable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2169-01-10 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We did an upper GI study this morning with contrast, and there’s no sign of a leak or blockage. That’s excellent news."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2169-01-10 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, that’s a relief. Can I start drinking now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2169-01-10 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll start with clear liquids — water, broth, apple juice — in small amounts. That’s stage one."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2169-01-10 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "How long will I stay on that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2169-01-10 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Usually a day or two. We’ll move you to pureed foods next, then soft solids. You’ll be on stage three by discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2169-01-10 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. What about my regular medications?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2169-01-10 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll resume them, but you’ll need to crush all pills for now — your stomach is smaller and can’t handle whole tablets."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2169-01-10 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Even my antidepressant and Abilify?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2169-01-10 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, all of them — citalopram, Abilify, lorazepam, and your pantoprazole for reflux. We’ll make sure they’re crushed and mixed with soft food."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2169-01-10 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing really well. We’re advancing your diet to stage three today — soft foods like mashed potatoes and scrambled eggs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2169-01-10 15:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That sounds good. I’m hungry but trying to go slow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2169-01-10 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Small, frequent meals — about ½ cup at a time. And no straws or gum — that can cause bloating."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2169-01-10 15:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t know that. Why no straws?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2169-01-10 15:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They can make you swallow air, which leads to bloating and discomfort. It’s best to avoid them for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2169-01-10 15:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good to know. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2169-01-11 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news — you’re cleared to go home today. You’ve tolerated stage three diet, your incisions are dry, and you’re walking well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2169-01-11 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What do I need to do when I get home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2169-01-11 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Stay on the stage three diet until your follow-up. Crush all pills, take your new meds — Protonix for reflux, Actigall for your gallbladder, and Colace for constipation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2169-01-11 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the pain medicine?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2169-01-11 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Roxicet as needed, but don’t drive or operate machinery — it can make you drowsy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2169-01-11 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll have my sister help me at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2169-01-11 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good idea. Also, no heavy lifting over 10 pounds for six weeks. You can shower, but no baths or swimming yet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2169-01-11 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if something goes wrong?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2169-01-11 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call us or go to the ER if you have a fever over 101.5, severe pain, vomiting, or redness around your incisions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2169-01-11 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll watch for that. Thank you for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2169-01-11 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. You did great. Follow up with Dr. Evans in two weeks. Take care."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2169-01-09 07:15:00",
    "admission_end": "2169-01-11 17:15:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for laparoscopic Roux-en-Y gastric bypass due to class III morbid obesity with a BMI of 40. She also had comorbid obstructive sleep apnea, gastroesophageal reflux, polycystic ovary syndrome, and fatty liver disease. The surgery was performed successfully, and she tolerated the procedure well. Postoperatively, an upper GI study confirmed no anastomotic leak, and her diet was advanced from clear liquids to stage three over the hospital stay. Pain was controlled with oral Roxicet, and she remained ambulatory. She was discharged home with instructions to continue crushed medications, follow a stage three diet, avoid straws and heavy lifting, and monitor for signs of complications. Follow-up was scheduled in two weeks.",
    "problems": [
      "Morbid obesity",
      "Body Mass Index 40 and over, adult",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Obstructive sleep apnea (adult)(pediatric)",
      "Polycystic ovaries",
      "Other chronic nonalcoholic liver disease"
    ]
  }
}
